Review:
This is a lovely soft dough to work with.  I preferred to make larger pitas so divided into fewer balls, rolled fairly thin between parchment, and baked at 445 convection for 6 minutes total, turning half way through.  Wrapped in a dish towel to keep warm, they flattened out and got softer as the next batch baked.  Quite easy, but a bit time consuming.  I used all purpose flour today, but think that it would be very good with part or all white whole wheat also.  Served with pork souvlaki (#39526
) and Tzatziki (#51983).  ( Kittencal's Famous Greek Salad (#66596
) would be a good compliment for a company meal.
